  "answer_text": "Great question \u2014 and it's genuinely debated! Here's a full breakdown:\n\n---\n\n## \ud83d\udc15 How to Pronounce \"Doge\"\n\nThere are **three common pronunciations**, and which one is \"correct\" depends on the context:\n\n---\n\n### 1. **\"Dohj\"** \u2014 /do\u028a\u0292/ *(Most widely accepted for the meme)*\nThis sounds like **\"vogue\"** but with a \"D\" \u2014 a soft \"zh\" sound at the end.\n\nThe most widely accepted pronunciation of Doge (as in the meme/Dogecoin) is **\"dohj\"**, written as /do\u028a\u0292/ in the International Phonetic Alphabet. This was confirmed by Dogecoin's co-creator Jackson Palmer.\n\nThe name was inspired by the animated series *Homestar Runner*, where a character spells out D-O-G-E and another character reads it as \"dohj\" (/do\u028a\u0292/).\n\n---\n\n### 2. **\"Doje\"** \u2014 /do\u028ad\u0292/ *(Also very common)*\nThis sounds like **\"dodge\"** but with a long \"O\" \u2014 rhymes with \"Scrooge\" sort of.\n\nAccording to Wikipedia, the meme can be pronounced /do\u028a\u0292/, /do\u028ad\u0292/, or /do\u028a\u0261/. The /do\u028ad\u0292/ version (like \"dodge\" with a long O) is very popular, especially in media.\n\n---\n\n### 3. **\"Dogg\"** or **\"Doggy\"** \u2014 /do\u028a\u0261/ *(Less common)*\nSome people simply pronounce it with a hard \"G,\" like the word \"dog\" with a long O, treating it as internet lolspeak for \"doggie.\"\n\nSince the word appears on a picture of a dog surrounded by lolspeak, some argue it should be pronounced with a hard \"G,\" similar to \"doggie.\"\n\n---\n\n### So what's the *actual* correct answer?\n\nSince \"Doge\" is a word that was practically made up for the purposes of an internet meme, it's no surprise that there's a lot of confusion about how to pronounce it.\n\nLanguage columnist Ben Zimmer favors /do\u028a\u0292/ or /do\u028ad\u0292/ (with the J sound) in deference to *Homestar Runner*. However, both the hard G (like \"dog\") and the soft G pronunciations are in common use and can be justified with reasonable explanations.\n\n**Bottom line:** If you want to say it the way the creators intended \u2192 say **\"dohj\"** (/do\u028a\u0292/). But **\"doje\"** (like dodge with a long O) is also totally acceptable and widely understood. You won't be wrong with either!",
